# Cloudflare Pages response headers (copied to the build root from /public).
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/

# Pages turns <link rel="modulepreload" href="chunk-….js"> into `Link:` headers
# (Early Hints). Browsers resolve header URLs against the page URL and ignore
# <base href="/">, so /about/ would preload /about/chunk-….js → 404.
# Angular already preloads the right URLs from the HTML, so drop the header.
/*
  ! Link
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Build output file names are content-hashed (outputHashing: all), so they
# never change in place and can be cached for a year.
/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
